{
 "cells": [
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "# Bosonic OPE Unit Tests\n\nBasic unit tests for OPE computations of fundamental bosonic worldsheet operators:\n- b-c ghost system\n- Matter fields (dX, dXt)\n- Composite operators (expX, ProfileX)",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "Needs[\"StringCode`\"]\nStringCode`InitStringCode[<|\"theory\" -> \"Bosonic\", \"CFT\" -> \"FlatSpace\", \"conventions\"-> \"Bosonic-Xi\", \"bracket\"->\"Flat\"|>]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## b-c Ghost System Tests\n\nThe b-c ghost system has the OPE:\n$$b(z) c(w) \\sim \frac{1}{z-w}$$\n$$c(z) b(w) \\sim \frac{1}{z-w}$$\n\nNote: Both orderings give the same propagator. The anticommutation is handled by normal ordering.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Test 1: Basic b-c contraction\n\nWick[b[0,z], c[0,w]] should give 1/(z-w)",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "test1 = Wick[b[0, z], c[0, w]];\nexpected1 = 1/(z - w);\ntest1Result = Simplify[test1 - expected1] === 0;\nPrint[\"Test 1 (b-c Wick): \", If[test1Result, \"PASSED\", \"FAILED\"]];\ntest1Result",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<pre>Test 1 (b-c Wick): PASSED\n</pre>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "\"Test 1 (b-c Wick): PASSED\\n\"",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "60e95ef7-7f1b-4c42-90c0-1fb8030474f1",
     "metadata": {
      "cellLabel": "",
      "isBoxData": false
     }
    },
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wexpr\"><w>True</w></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "True",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "de839fe7-e034-4ccc-8e69-d8fc83a302b1",
     "metadata": {
      "cellLabel": "Out[7]= ",
      "isBoxData": false
     }
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Test 2: c-b contraction (same sign as b-c)\n\nWick[c[0,z], b[0,w]] should give 1/(z-w)",
