  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Test 23: OPE of R[dX, dXt] with R[expX]\n\nBoth dX and dXt contract independently with expX, producing two singular terms (one in z-w, one in zbar-wbar).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "test23 = OPE[R[dX[\\[Mu], 0, z], dXt[\\[Nu], 0, zbar]], R[expX[k, w, wbar]]];\nPrint[\"Test 23 (OPE R[dX,dXt]-expX): \", test23 // InputForm];\n(* Should have poles in both z-w and zbar-wbar *)\ntest23HasHoloPole = Not[FreeQ[test23, 1/(z - w)]] || Not[FreeQ[test23, 1/(w - z)]];\ntest23HasAntiHoloPole = Not[FreeQ[test23, 1/(zbar - wbar)]] || Not[FreeQ[test23, 1/(wbar - zbar)]];\ntest23Result = test23HasHoloPole && test23HasAntiHoloPole;\nPrint[\"Test 23 (has both holo and anti-holo poles): \", If[test23Result, \"PASSED\", \"FAILED\"]];\ntest23Result",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<pre>Test 23 (OPE R[dX,dXt]-expX): ((-1/2*I)*Î±p*k[Î½]*\n \n&gt;       R[dX[Î¼, 0, z], expX[k, w, wbar]])/(-wbar + zbar) - \n \n&gt;    (I/2*Î±p*k[Î¼]*(((-1/2*I)*Î±p*k[Î½]*R[expX[k, w, wbar]])/\n \n&gt;          (-wbar + zbar) + R[dXt[Î½, 0, zbar], expX[k, w, wbar]]))/(-w + z)\\\n \n&gt;     + R[dX[Î¼, 0, z], dXt[Î½, 0, zbar], expX[k, w, wbar]]\n</pre>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
